WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.691
Learn to construct different rectangles for a given area (cm2 or m2) in order to

00:00:05.691 --> 00:00:09.352
demonstrate that many different rectangles may have the same area

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:16.477
A rectangle has area 10 cm squared and length 2 cm. What is the width? The answer is

00:00:16.477 --> 00:00:19.267
5 cm. 10 divided by 2 equals 5.

00:00:20.117 --> 00:00:25.765
A rectangular plot is 3 m by 3 m. What total area does the plot cover? Pause and

00:00:25.765 --> 00:00:27.647
solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.674
The answer is 9 m squared total. 3 times 3 equals 9.
